      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-182346",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\mid R|= c$, complete the following reasoning about the cardinality of the set $[0, 2)\u222a[3, \u221e)$:\n\nSince the function $f: x \u2192 x$ (that maps any number to itself) is an injection from $[0, 2)\u222a[3, \u221e)$ into $R$, and\n$\\tan (x)$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nis an injection from $R$ onto $(0, 2)\u2286[0, 2)\u222a[3, \u221e)$, according to Cantor-Bernstein-Schr\u00f6der theorem, we have that\n$\\mid [0, 2)\u222a[3, \u221e)|=$ {{field-3}}."
