      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-183611",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $\\mid R|= c$, complete the following reasoning about the cardinality of the set $[- 3,-1)\u222a(3, 5)$:\n\nSince the function $f: x \u2192 x$ (that maps any number to itself) is an injection from $[- 3,-1)\u222a(3, 5)$ into $R$, and\n$\\arctan (x)$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nis an injection from $R$ onto $(-3,-1)\u2286[- 3,-1)\u222a(3, 5)$, according to Cantor-Bernstein-Schr\u00f6der theorem, we have that\n$\\mid [- 3,-1)\u222a(3, 5)|=$ {{field-3}}."
